PATCH 388: SETTINGS AUTO TURRET CONTROL toggle -- LED re-renders on toggle (store-width, patch-318/319/387 class).

Same class as 387: the AUTO TURRET CONTROL checkbox toggle FUN_0000_6be7 (asm 0x6be7 `xorb [0x8b4d]`,
0x6bec `movb [0x8bbe],3`, posts msgid 0x174b ENABLED / 0x172e DISABLED via 7018) flips its state + status
line correctly but the LED indicator did not re-render -- its two flags were left WORD-typed while the
318/319/387 sweeps retyped the neighbours:
  - state flag 0x8b4d (DAT_2000_4b4d): asm xor/cmp BYTE; WORD typing pulls in adjacent 0x8b4e.
  - dirty flag 0x8bbe (uRam00024bbe): asm `movb $3` BYTE; WORD `=3` clobbers the renderer-index byte
    0x8bbf -> the dirty-walk (209e) dispatched the wrong renderer -> the AUTO TURRET indicator (6d27,
    the inverted-checkbox renderer that reads byte[0x8b4d]) never re-ran.
Retype both to undefined1, matching the asm.  SETTINGS-click-only -> behaviour-neutral for all other flows.
Verified: AUTO TURRET toggle AE=0 vs DOSBox oracle native AND wasm, native<->wasm 0-diff.  re_out pristine.

